# Secrets never enter the build context: `container-publish` uploads the
# context to a REMOTE Docker Build Cloud builder, so an unexcluded .env
# would leave the machine on every build even though no layer COPYs it.
.env
data/
models/
results/
references/
.venv
# Nested venvs need an explicit `**` — a bare `.venv` pattern is matched against
# the path relative to the build context ROOT, so it excludes only the top-level
# one. Agent worktrees under .claude/worktrees/ each carry a full ~1.3G venv
# (torch dominates); MEASURED mid-sprint with 7 of them resident: 9.1G of a 10G
# context, none of it excluded. Those directories are also build-context-only
# noise — nothing in either image is built from them.
**/.venv
.claude/
.codex/
.git
.dvc/tmp
.dvc/cache
__pycache__
*.pyc
.pytest_cache
.ruff_cache
.mypy_cache
.env
notebooks/
